<title>CANADA: Unions reiterate opposition to Canadian plan.</title>
<headline>Unions reiterate opposition to Canadian plan.</headline>
<dateline>VANCOUVER 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leaders of the Canadian Union of Public Employees (CUPE) and the Canadian Auto Workers (CAW) union, the two unions opposed to Canadian Airlines Corp's restructuring plans, repeated on Monday their opposition to wage cuts proposed by the airline's management.</p>
<p>The union leaders made the comments before a meeting with federal Transport Minister David Anderson.</p>
<p>Anderson and Canadian Airlines president Kevin Benson said earlier today that the support of the two unions was crucial if the restructuring plan was to advance, but CUPE and CAW officials were unmoved. &quot;We're not giving any more,&quot; said CAW president Buzz Hargrove.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Toronto Bureau  (416) 941-8100</p>
